{"book": "gate-da", "num": 14, "label": "14", "slug": "14-matrices-special-matrices", "title": "Special Matrices", "tag": "Matrices & Linear Algebra", "summary": "A projection matrix $P$ is a square matrix that satisfies", "wordCount": 353, "readingTimeMin": 2, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "14.1", "title": "Projection Matrices", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A <b>projection matrix</b> $P$ is a square matrix that satisfies"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P^2 = P."}, {"t": "p", "x": "It \"projects\" a vector onto a subspace. If $v$ is any vector, $Pv$ is the projection of $v$ onto the subspace.\nProperties:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Eigenvalues of $P$ are 0 or 1."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$I - P$ is also a projection matrix."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $P$ is symmetric ($P^T = P$), it is an orthogonal projection."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "101", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Let"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Check if $P$ is a projection matrix: $P^2 = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} = P$."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "102", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "For"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P = \\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix},"}, {"t": "p", "x": "compute $P^2 = \\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix} = P$. So $P$ is a projection matrix."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "103", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Check if $I-P$ is also a projection:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "I-P = \\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & -0.5 \\\\ -0.5 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad (I-P)^2 = I-P."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus, $I-P$ is a projection onto orthogonal subspace."}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}]}, {"id": "14.2", "title": "Orthogonal Matrices", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A square matrix $Q$ is <b>orthogonal</b> if"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q^T Q = QQ^T = I."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Properties:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$Q^{-1} = Q^T$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Determinant: $\\det(Q) = \\pm 1$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Columns (and rows) of $Q$ form an orthonormal set."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Eigenvalues satisfy $|\\lambda| = 1$."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "104", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "Q = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad Q^T Q = I."}, {"t": "p", "x": "So $Q$ is orthogonal."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "105", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "Q = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad Q^T Q = I."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Columns are orthonormal, determinant = 1."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "106", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Check inverse: $Q^{-1} = Q^T = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$."}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}]}, {"id": "14.3", "title": "Orthogonal", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A real square matrix $A$ is called <b>orthogonal</b> if"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A^T = A^{-1}, \\quad \\text{or equivalently } AA^T = A^T A = I."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus, $A$ must be invertible and its rows and columns form orthonormal sets of vectors."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "107", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "A = \\frac{1}{9}\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n8 & 4 & 9 \\\\\n4 & 9 & -9 \\\\\n9 & -9 & -4\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "It can be verified that $AA^T = I = A^T A$.\nHence, $A^T = A^{-1}$ and $A$ is orthogonal."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Properties of Orthogonal Matrices:</b>"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": false, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The rows of an orthogonal matrix form an orthonormal set."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "The columns of an orthogonal matrix form an orthonormal set."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "If $A$ is orthogonal, then $\\det(A) = \\pm 1$."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "108", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "For $n=2$, every real orthogonal matrix has the form"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}\n\\cos \\theta & \\sin \\theta \\\\\n-\\sin \\theta & \\cos \\theta\n\\end{bmatrix}\n\\quad \\text{or} \\quad\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}\n\\cos \\theta & \\sin \\theta \\\\\n\\sin \\theta & -\\cos \\theta\n\\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Both are orthogonal since $AA^T = I$."}]}]}, {"id": "14.4", "title": "Normal", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A real square matrix $A$ is called <b>normal</b> if it commutes with its transpose:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "AA^T = A^T A."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Every symmetric, skew-symmetric, and orthogonal matrix is normal."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "109", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "A =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n3 & -3 \\\\\n-3 & 3\n\\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Then"}, {"t": "math", "x": "AA^T =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n45 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 45\n\\end{bmatrix},\n\\quad\nA^T A =\n\\begin{bmatrix}\n45 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 45\n\\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Since $AA^T = A^T A$, the matrix $A$ is normal."}]}]}, {"id": "14.5", "title": "Idempotent Matrices", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "A matrix $A$ is <b>idempotent</b> if"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A^2 = A."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Properties:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Eigenvalues are 0 or 1."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "$I-A$ is also idempotent."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Rank$(A) = \\text{tr}(A)$ if $A$ is symmetric."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "110", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad A^2 = A."}, {"t": "p", "x": "So $A$ is idempotent."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "111", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad A^2 = A."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Hence idempotent."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "112", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Check $I-A$:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "I-A = \\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & -0.5 \\\\ -0.5 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad (I-A)^2 = I-A."}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}]}, {"id": "14.6", "title": "Partition (Block) Matrices", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Matrices can be partitioned into submatrices (blocks):"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}A_{11} & A_{12} \\\\ A_{21} & A_{22}\\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Block properties:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Block multiplication: conformable sizes."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Determinant of block-diagonal: $\\det(A) = \\det(A_{11})\\det(A_{22})$."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Useful for LU decomposition or large systems."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "113", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{bmatrix} & \\begin{bmatrix}1\\\\2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & \\begin{bmatrix}5\\end{bmatrix} \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Matrix is partitioned into 4 blocks."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "114", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "For block-diagonal"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}B & 0 \\\\ 0 & C\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\det(A) = \\det(B)\\det(C)."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "115", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Block multiplication:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{bmatrix}A & B \\\\ C & D\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}X & Y \\\\ Z & W\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}AX + BZ & AY + BW \\\\ CX + DZ & CY + DW\\end{bmatrix}."}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}]}, {"id": "14.7", "title": "Properties of Special Matrices", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Summary of key properties:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Projection and idempotent: $P^2 = P$, eigenvalues = 0 or 1."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Orthogonal: $Q^T Q = I$, inverse = transpose, determinant = ±1."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Block matrices: useful in partitioned operations, determinant of block-diagonal = product of determinants."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Symmetric idempotent: rank = trace."}]}]}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "116", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Symmetric idempotent:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \\text{rank}(A) = \\text{tr}(A) = 1."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "117", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Orthogonal check:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "Q = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad Q^T Q = I, \\det(Q)=-1."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "118", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Projection matrix property:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "P = \\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & 0.5 \\\\ 0.5 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad I-P = \\begin{bmatrix}0.5 & -0.5 \\\\ -0.5 & 0.5\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad (I-P)^2 = I-P."}]}, {"t": "p", "x": "—"}]}, {"id": "14.8", "title": "Applications of Special Matrices", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Applications:"}, {"t": "list", "ordered": true, "style": null, "desc": false, "items": [{"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Projection matrices: least squares, computer graphics."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Orthogonal matrices: rotations, reflections, numerical stability."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Idempotent matrices: statistics (hat matrices), regression analysis."}]}, {"blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Block matrices: large-scale computation, parallel processing, solving partitioned systems."}]}]}]}]}], "sectionCount": 8}